    {
      "id": 283,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -426.1866760253906,
        1100.1630859375
      ],
      "size": [
        352.0401916503906,
        650.5386352539062
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 18,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "This is for copying face styles from an image to another person and I added in controlnet feature to keep face structure as I was using it to make characters for lora training in Wan.\n\n\njust stick a face image in \"Load Image 1\" node. Set 1 entry\nand put your target image in Load image on right of it and then right cliuck the target image and mask edit the face (or whatever you want restyled).\n\nreduce denoise to 0.4 or 0.5, or make it 1.0 if you want it totally overwriting the face not merging into the old one\n\nthen run it. make sure prompt is something like: \n\n\"Maintain likeness. photograph featuring the same man with face at different angle.\"\n\nthe original lora was Ace_PLUS_portrait but I think that is the same as comfyui protrait lora64 I am using.\nif doing other things like clothes, change the lora to compatible ones for ACE++, I use comfyui_subject_lora16.safetensors for clothing swaps.\n\n\nthis workflow originally came from here - https://www.reddit.com/r/comfyui/comments/1iwv4yw/comment/meh713s/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web3x&utm_name=web3xcss&utm_term=1&utm_content=share_button\n\nface swaps in about 5 mins on my 3060\n\n---\n\nUSING CONTROLNET:\n\neither plug Set_1 or Set_2 (depending which you want to keep face structure) into the AIO Aux PReprocessor and choose your controlnet.\n\nset the same controlnet in the \"Setunionconteolnet\" node.\nit seems fiddly but its not.\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
